{
  "id": 188163949,
  "iid": 8827,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "tcp: Use correct wraparound comparison in sequence analysis",
  "description": "maxseqtobeacked needs to be increased when it's lower than nextseq, not the other way around, otherwise we can get repeated extra TCP ACKed unseen segment messages.\n    \nSince sequence analysis is always on the absolute sequence numbers, not relative, it needs to use LT_SEQ to handle wraparound.\n    \nFix #18558. Fix #18633.",
