      "resolved": true,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1171862705,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Hmm. I think not only do the wraparound aware comparisons need to be used, but shouldn't the comparison be the other way around?\n\n@eugene.adell, you made the change above, but shouldn't `maxseqtobeacked` be updated when there's an ACK of a lost packet and it's _less_ than nextseq, not greater than? (The logic being that in the previous reverse direction packet, `maxseqtobeacked` wasn't updated because the sequence number didn't match the previous `nextseq` (but the reverse `nextseq` is always updated.)",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
